---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import PresentationFigure from "../components/PresentationFigure.astro";
import Comparison from "../components/Comparison.astro";
import Citation from "../components/Citation.astro";
import MediaCredit from "../components/MediaCredit.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
const sections = ["Abstract", "Method", "Experiments", "Results", "Citation"];
---

<Layout>
  <Hero />
  <div class="container visual-overview">
    <nav class="research-nav" aria-label="Research sections"><ol>{sections.map((name) => <li><a href={`#${name.toLowerCase()}`}>{name}</a></li>)}</ol></nav>
    <section class="section abstract-section" id="abstract" aria-labelledby="abstract-title">
      <h2 id="abstract-title">Abstract</h2>
      <p>Human-driven and robot vehicles will share urban roads during the transition to autonomous driving. We study how learned vehicle control can coexist with conventional traffic signals across a 14-intersection network in Colorado Springs. A shared Rainbow DQN policy lets robot vehicles choose Stop or Go from local traffic observations. In SUMO, we vary robot-vehicle penetration and the number of unsignalized intersections. Selected combinations reduce waiting time and increase destination arrivals, but replacing more signals does not guarantee improvement. The results support evaluating the transition at both network and individual-intersection scales.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <h2 id="method-title">Method</h2>
      <p class="section-deck">Observe local traffic. Choose Stop or Go. Coordinate through shared roads.</p>
      <PresentationFigure id="method" concise />
      <p>Robot vehicles use Rainbow DQN within a 30 m control zone and the Intelligent Driver Model elsewhere. Human-driven vehicles follow IDM.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={asset("paper/#guide-2")}>Observation, action & reward details →</a>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="experiments" aria-labelledby="experiments-title">
      <h2 id="experiments-title">Experiments</h2>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>Intersections</dt><dd>14</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Control configurations</dt><dd>5</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Robot vehicles</dt><dd>40–80%</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <Figure id="network" concise />
      <div class="intersection-grid"><PresentationFigure id="signalized" concise /><PresentationFigure id="unsignalized" concise /></div>
      <p>Five configurations combine 2–10 robot-managed intersections with conventional signals. The baseline retains all 14 signals.</p>
      <details class="reading-details"><summary>Experiment protocol & simulation scope</summary>
        {site.guideSections[2].paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{text}</p>)}
        <p>The opening SUMO recording illustrates the setting; it does not identify a controller or robot-vehicle rate. Waymo footage provides independent real-world context.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
      <h2 id="results-title">Results</h2>
      <p class="section-deck">At 80% robot vehicles, 8U + 6S improves both network metrics.</p>
      <div class="highlights">{site.highlights.map((item) => <div><><h3>{item.label}</h3><p class="numeric-pair"><><span>{item.before}</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="sr-only">to</span><strong>{item.after}</strong></></p></></div>)}</div>
      <p class="fine-print">Fully signalized baseline → 8U + 6S. Throughput: destination arrivals per 500 s.</p>
      <Figure id="penetration" concise />
      <p>Gains depend on the configuration and penetration rate. Some intersections retain lower waiting times under traffic signals.</p>
      <details class="reading-details" id="comparison-details"><summary>Compare configurations & review limitations</summary>
        <Comparison />
        <p>At 50% robot vehicles, 6U + 8S increases waiting to 7.92 s and lowers throughput to 448, versus 6.17 s and 454 for the baseline.</p>
        <ul>{site.limitations.map((text) => <li>{text}</li>)}</ul>
      </details>
      <a class="button dark" href={asset("results/")}>Full results & CSV data →</a>
    </section>
    <Citation />
    <details class="reading-details media-details" id="media-descriptions"><summary>Video descriptions & sources</summary><MediaCredit /></details>
  </div>
</Layout>
